<!--
  The moment (PRD-07 T6 and T7): the platform says "this happened to this player" and the
  server shows it. A slim toast for everybody on one of three rows at the right edge, and
  for the person a card at the left edge that slides in face down and turns over. The
  plugin's `Moments` (plugins/EZPug.Sdk/Hud/Moments.cs) drives it and names every id and
  class below; docs/hud.md, "The moment", is the table.

  Half time (PRD-09 T4) is a band at the top of the screen for everybody, standing for the
  whole break while both sides can hear each other; its words are each player's language.

  The unboxing (PRD-08 T3, redrawn in PRD-09 T8) is the last panel: a drop with a reel,
  played for everybody at the top of the screen in a freeze. The call (the winner's name
  and "hat einen Drop!"), a reel of 36 slots the server steps past the marker, fast and
  then slower, to a stop on the prize, then the prize, grown and tinted. ezpug_unbox.css
  says which slot the reel stops on and every class. The label without an id in the
  reel's window is the addon's build stamp, written by `pnpm hud:build` (hud/src/stamp.ts).

  Every label binds `{s:text}` and the server sets it on the label's own id. The card's
  picture is a class on #moment_card (`art-<key>`, ezpug_art.css); no class, or a key this
  addon does not hold, is the empty sleeve. A tier is a class too (`tier-<name>`), on the
  card for the person and on a toast's row for everybody.

  Rules every layout in hud/layout/ keeps (docs/hud.md, the Findings of ralph/PRD-07-hud.md):
  - the root panel carries no id; the server addresses the panels inside it;
  - only Panel, Label, Image and Button; pictures are backgrounds, never <Image>;
  - no inline style; nothing takes the mouse (hittest="false" everywhere).
-->
